      "agent_input": "I'd like to read the Q3 2026 business report, please.",
      "agent_response": {
        "response": "Here's the **Meridian Analytics \u2014 Q3 2026 Business Report**:\n\n---\n\n**Period:** July 1 \u2013 September 7, 2026\n**Prepared by:** Rachel Kim, VP of Sales | Claire Fontaine, CFO\n**Distribution:** Executive Team\n\n---\n\n### Executive Summary\n\nQ3 2026 marks another strong quarter for Meridian Analytics. Across the 15-person team, **14 deals were closed out of 22 opportunities**, generating **$1,040,000** in new contract value. The sales pipeline remains healthy with several high-value deals still pending, and all critical customer support issues were resolved same-day.\n\n---\n\n### Sales Performance\n\n- **Total closed revenue:** $1,040,000\n- **Top region:** South \u2014 $468,000 in won deals\n- **Sales team:** James Okafor, Sofia Delgado, and Marcus Webb worked 22 active opportunities\n- **Product mix:** Shifted toward *Meridian Insights Pro* (majority of closed revenue); *Meridian DataBridge* remains a strong land-and-expand vehicle\n- **Win rate:** 63.6% (above the 55% company target)\n- **Pending deals:** ~$240,000 across three deals expected to close by end of September\n\n---\n\n### Key Highlights\n\n- **Top deal:** Sofia Delgado closed a **$198,000** Meridian Insights Pro contract with a Southern-region enterprise customer on September 5 (D019)\n- **Team headcount:** 15 employees across 5 departments \u2014 Sales (4), Engineering (5), Product (3), HR (1), Finance (2)\n- **Support SLA:** All critical-priority tickets (TKT-004, TKT-011, TKT-015) resolved within 24 hours\n- **License utilisation:** SKU-001 (Meridian Insights Pro) at **94% capacity** \u2014 procurement review scheduled for October\n\n---\n\n### Next Steps\n\n1. Close the pending deals (D007, D013, D020, D022) before Q3 end\n2. Begin Q4 pipeline review \u2014 target **$1.2M** in new ARR\n3. Resolve open support tickets (TKT-013, TKT-016, TKT-019) ahead of quarterly customer success calls\n4. Conduct license capacity review for SKU-001 and SKU-003 in early October\n5. HR to initiate two new engineering hire approvals with Kenji Obi to support the Q4 roadmap\n\n---\n\nLet me know if you'd like to dive deeper into any section or cross-reference the underlying sales or expense data!",
        "status_code": null
      },
